{"name":"Captain Nemo","hex":"#828080","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"captain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chief or leader.","The person lawfully in command of a ship or other vessel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act as captain","To exercise command of a ship, aircraft or sports team."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captain"},{"term":"nemo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Acronym of not emanating from main office, i.e. broadcast from some remote location instead."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nemo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Captain Nemo","blocks":[{"text":"Captain Nemo is a character created by the French novelist Jules Verne (1828–1905). Nemo appears in two of Verne's science-fiction books, Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas (1870) and The Mysterious Island (1875). He also makes a brief appearance in a play written by Verne with the collaboration of Adolphe d'Ennery, Journey Through the Impossible (1882)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%27Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea%27_by_Neuville_and_Riou_027.jpg/330px-%27Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea%27_by_Neuville_and_Riou_027.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_Nemo","wikidata":"Q1046049"},{"title":"Captain Nemo (miniseries)","blocks":[{"text":"Captain Nemo is a 1975 Soviet three-part television miniseries directed by Vasily Levin loosely based on the Jules Verne novels Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas (1870), its 1874 sequel The Mysterious Island, and The Steam House (1880)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Captain_Nemo_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_Nemo_(miniseries)","wikidata":"Q4212947"},{"title":"Captain","blocks":[{"text":"Captain is a title, an appellative for the commanding officer of a military unit; the commander or highest rank officer of a navy ship, merchant ship, aeroplane, spacecraft, or other vessel; or the commander of a port, fire or police department, election precinct, etc. In militaries, the captain is typically at the level of an officer commanding a company or battalion of infantry, a ship, or a battery of artillery, or another distinct unit. It can also be a rank of command in an air force. The term also may be used as an informal or honorary title for persons in similar commanding roles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Captain_on_ship.jpg/330px-Captain_on_ship.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain","wikidata":"Q25114211"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/OrchhaPalace.jpg/500px-OrchhaPalace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/OrchhaPalace.jpg/1280px-OrchhaPalace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/OrchhaPalace.jpg/500px-OrchhaPalace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orchha Fort complex, home to the real-life rajas of Orchha, Bundelkhand.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrchhaPalace.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/20000_Nemo_organ.jpg/500px-20000_Nemo_organ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/20000_Nemo_organ.jpg/1280px-20000_Nemo_organ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/20000_Nemo_organ.jpg/500px-20000_Nemo_organ.jp